{
  "metadata": {
    "source": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing",
    "last_verified": "2026-08-13",
    "currency": "USD",
    "schema_version": "1",
    "conventions": {
      "price_entry_shape": {
        "price": "number (USD)",
        "unit": "always 'USD'",
        "billing_unit": "per_1M_tokens",
        "dimension": "input | input_cache_hit | cache_writes | output"
      },
      "lookup_key_pattern": "{canonical_model_id}#{tier}#{dimension}",
      "tier_values": "standard | batch | long_context_standard | long_context_batch | fast_mode | long_context_fast_mode",
      "resolution_flow": "any_string -> model_string_index -> canonical_id -> lookup key",
      "cache_note": "Cached input (automatic prompt caching) billed at input_cache_hit price; non-cached input at input price. Reasoning/'pro' models do not expose a cached-input rate — cached tokens fall back to the full input price in PriceManager.",
      "cache_writes_note": "gpt-5.6-sol/terra/luna are the only models that publish a distinct cache_writes rate (cost of newly writing a segment into the prompt cache, separate from cache_hit reads). Sourced directly for the standard and long_context_standard tiers; batch and long_context_batch cache_writes entries are derived as standard x 0.5 / long_context_standard x 0.5 (source did not publish a batch cache_writes rate — see batch_note). Models without a captured cache_writes entry (all non-gpt-5.6 models) simply have no cache-write billing dimension; PriceManager should treat any provided cache-write token count as $0.00 for those models rather than erroring.",
      "batch_note": "Batch API (async) is a uniform 50% discount on input, cached input, cache_writes, and output. Batch entries are derived as standard x 0.5.",
      "long_context_note": "long_context_standard / long_context_batch / long_context_fast_mode apply when total prompt tokens > 272,000 (the long_context threshold); PriceManager switches to these keys automatically when the model publishes them (see gpt_5_6_coverage_note). Below the threshold, standard / batch / fast_mode apply. standard/batch published for gpt-5.4-pro and every model at or above it in the GPT-5.x line (gpt-5.4-pro, gpt-5.4, gpt-5.5-pro, gpt-5.5, gpt-5.6-sol, gpt-5.6-terra, gpt-5.6-luna); earlier/smaller models (gpt-5.4-mini, gpt-5.4-nano, gpt-5.3-codex, chatgpt-latest, gpt-5.6-cyber) do not publish a long-context rate. fast_mode/long_context_fast_mode are gpt-5.6-sol/terra/luna only.",
      "fast_mode_note": "fast_mode is a distinct, higher-throughput service tier published only for gpt-5.6-sol/terra/luna, priced at exactly 2x the corresponding standard/long_context_standard rate across every dimension (input, input_cache_hit, cache_writes, output) for all three models — sourced directly, not derived, but the 2x ratio is exact and can be used to sanity-check future updates. There is no fast_mode_batch variant; fast_mode and batch are mutually exclusive service tiers. Naming: this tier was called 'Priority processing' before being renamed 'Fast mode' on 2026-07-30; the API request parameter service_tier accepts either \"priority\" or \"fast\" for the same tier (same pricing, same lookup key 'fast_mode' in this schema) — PriceManager.calculate_cost accepts tier values \"fast_mode\", \"fast\", or \"priority\" interchangeably.",
      "gpt_5_5_pro_batch_note": "Source page returned an anomalous batch rate for gpt-5.5-pro (higher than standard); corrected to the standard 50% discount, matching its sibling gpt-5.4-pro.",
      "coverage_note": "Only the GPT-5.x generation (plus chatgpt-latest and gpt-5.3-codex) is listed on the developer pricing page. Earlier families (gpt-4.1, gpt-4o, o3, o4-mini) were not present and are intentionally omitted.",
      "gpt_5_6_coverage_note": "gpt-5.6-sol/terra/luna source data also publishes a flex tier. flex is numerically identical to batch for every gpt-5.6 model, so it is intentionally omitted — PriceManager maps tier='flex' straight onto the batch lookup keys, losing no information. fast_mode and cache_writes (previously dropped) are now fully captured — see fast_mode_note and cache_writes_note. gpt-5.6-cyber's source only publishes a standard short_context tier (no batch, no long_context, no fast_mode). long_context_batch entries for gpt-5.4-pro/gpt-5.4/gpt-5.5-pro/gpt-5.5 are derived as long_context_standard x 0.5 (source did not publish batch or long_context_batch rates directly for these models, but every other batch entry in this file matches this ratio exactly)."
    }
  },
